>> title: 3rd Saturday in October Chili
>> description: Makes 1 gallon. Use at least a 6 quart pot.
>> author: Sinda Snead
>> course: dinner
>> cuisine: American
>> tags: chili, game day

In a #large pot{}, brown @ground beef{5%lbs}. When the meat is almost done, add chopped @onion{1%large} and cook, stirring often, until the onions brown and are glazed.

Skim the grease from the top. Stir in @taco seasoning mix{2%1.25 oz pkg} and @chili seasoning mix{2%1.25 oz pkg}. Add @tomato sauce{2%15 oz cans}, @diced tomatoes{1%14.5 oz can} (no salt), @mild picante sauce{8%oz}, and all the beans, strained: @red kidney beans{2%15.5 oz cans} and @chili hot beans{2%16 oz cans}.

Rinse the cans with a tiny amount of water and add it until the chili looks right, if it even needs any to begin with.

Simmer for ~{10%minutes}. Add @Jack Daniel's whiskey{4%oz} and return to a simmer for ~{10%minutes}.

Serve over @corn chips{} and sprinkle @grated cheese{} on top if desired.
